> zoi gy. Grice gy. mo?

Philosopher responsible for the influential idea that
utterance interpretation is a product of literal sentence
meaning and very general principles that apply to
communication in general, and not to any specific language.
[It may seem an obvious idea, but if you read linguistics from
pre 1970s you realize that at the time it wasn't.] He had more
to say than this, and more specific proposals, but this, I
take it, is roughly what we mean by 'Gricean'.

